UNIT carried_canonical
LANG rust
PRIMARY-SHA256 f0f8bfd7fcf65ee10da915c5044801760095bf39afc82f9b18fe04a03e3cf1a3
SIG pub fn carried_canonical(table: &serde_json::Value) -> String
ABI crate shape: the artifact is a LIBRARY crate ([lib], src/lib.rs exporting pub fn carried_canonical) depending on
  serde_json only — no main, no I/O, no unsafe. The verifier's generated harness parses one JSON args line per stdin line,
  binds `table` as a serde_json::Value::Object, calls carried_canonical(&table), and prints the String; a panic is a throw.
ABI type mapping: map = Value::Object (serde_json::Map<String, Value>); json = Value; none = Value::Null; bool =
  Value::Bool; text = Value::String; list = Value::Array; f64 = Value::Number, read with as_f64 (an integer Number from
  the harness is an exact double, since every number the oracle holds is one).
ENVELOPE narrowing: serde_json::Value holds no NaN, infinity or negative zero, so R6 is unreachable here: the harness
  narrows every vector carrying one (R6 is graded in js and ts only). Lone surrogates have no String form (already OUT in
  the primary). With R6 unreachable the function never fails on a Value it can receive; it returns String, no Result.
MECHANISM key order (R2): NEVER rely on serde_json::Map iteration order at ANY depth — without preserve_order it is a
  BTreeMap in byte / code-point order, with it the arrival order. Collect each map's keys (top level AND nested) and sort
  them by `a.encode_utf16().cmp(b.encode_utf16())` — str's own Ord is code-point order and misplaces astral keys against
  the top of the basic plane. Digit-only keys get no special treatment.
MECHANISM numbers (R5): a zero (integer 0 or 0.0) is "0". Do NOT use serde_json's number writer or `{}`/`{:?}` (they print 1e21 as "1e21" or
  "1000000000000000000000" and 255.0 as "255.0"). Take the shortest round-trip digits from `format!("{:e}", x.abs())`
  (mantissa digits with the point removed = d, exponent + 1 = n) and lay them out by the primary's R5 cases, prefixing
  "-" when x < 0.
MECHANISM text (R4): escape by hand per R4 (or serde_json::to_string on the &str, whose escape set and lowercase hex
  match R4); keys are sorted on the raw String, never on the escaped form.
DEPENDS-ON none
PROVENANCE rederive@b15b56613f9d cli/sir/v05.mjs `canonical`. Language file re-cut 2026-10-26 with the primary;
  the ABI follows the lab's rust driver (drivers/rust.mjs: map/json arrive as serde_json::Value, NaN/Inf/-0 narrowed).
